    "id": "NDDI",
    "summary": "Calculates the Normalized Difference Dust Index (NDDI) from Sentinel-2 data.",
    "description": "The Normalized Difference Dust Index (NDDI) is a spectral index designed to detect sand and dust storms (SDS) from optical satellite imagery. It was proposed by Qu et al. (2006) for MODIS data as a simple way to identify dust storms and separate them from clouds using only solar reflectance bands.\n\n**Why it works**\n\nMineral dust (sand and soil particles) has a characteristic spectral signature: its reflectance is low in the blue part of the spectrum and increases with wavelength towards the shortwave infrared (SWIR). Clouds, by contrast, are bright in both regions, so their reflectance is similar in the blue and in the SWIR. Taking the normalized difference between a SWIR band and a blue band therefore gives high values for dust and values close to or below zero for clouds.\n\n**Formula**\n\nNDDI = (ρSWIR − ρBlue) / (ρSWIR + ρBlue)\n\nThe original MODIS formulation uses the 2.13 µm band and the 0.469 µm band. In this process the Sentinel-2 equivalents are used: B12 (SWIR, ~2.19 µm) and B02 (blue, ~0.49 µm).\n\n**Interpretation**\n\n- NDDI < 0: typically clouds.\n- NDDI > 0.28: dust storm, the threshold reported in the original study for MODIS over East Asia.\n- Values in between: dust-free surfaces or thin or mixed conditions.\n\nBare ground can also give relatively high values, so it may need a higher, region-specific threshold (later studies report about 0.46 over the Yellow River Basin). The thresholds come from MODIS top-of-atmosphere data and should be checked and calibrated before being applied to Sentinel-2 surface reflectance (L2A).\n\n**Applications**\n\nNDDI is used to detect and map dust storms, track their extent and transport over time, and identify dust over bright surfaces such as deserts, where aerosol optical thickness products are often unavailable. Its main limitations are confusion with bare soil and sensitivity to surface brightness and atmospheric correction.\n\n**About this process**\n\nThis process computes NDDI from Sentinel-2 L2A data for the given spatial and temporal extent. It returns two bands: 'NDDI' and 'cloudy_pixels', a mask derived from the Scene Classification Layer (SCL classes 8, 9 and 10: medium and high probability cloud, and thin cirrus).\n\n**Reference**\n\nQu, J. J., Hao, X., Kafatos, M., & Wang, L. (2006). Asian Dust Storm Monitoring Combining Terra and Aqua MODIS SRB Measurements. IEEE Geoscience and Remote Sensing Letters, 3(4), 484–486. https://doi.org/10.1109/LGRS.2006.877752",
    "parameters": [
        {
            "name": "spatial_extent",
            "description": "Limits the data to process to the specified bounding box or polygons.\\n\\nFor raster data, the process loads the pixel into the data cube if the point at the pixel center intersects with the bounding box or any of the polygons (as defined in the Simple Features standard by the OGC).\\nFor vector data, the process loads the geometry into the data cube if the geometry is fully within the bounding box or any of the polygons (as defined in the Simple Features standard by the OGC). Empty geometries may only be in the data cube if no spatial extent has been provided.\\n\\nEmpty geometries are ignored.\\nSet this parameter to null to set no limit for the spatial extent.",
            "schema": [
                {
                    "title": "Bounding Box",
                    "type": "object",
                    "subtype": "bounding-box",
                    "required": [
                        "west",
                        "south",
                        "east",
                        "north"
                    ],
                    "properties": {
                        "west": {
                            "description": "West (lower left corner, coordinate axis 1).",
                            "type": "number"
                        },
                        "south": {
                            "description": "South (lower left corner, coordinate axis 2).",
                            "type": "number"
                        },
                        "east": {
                            "description": "East (upper right corner, coordinate axis 1).",
                            "type": "number"
                        },
                        "north": {
                            "description": "North (upper right corner, coordinate axis 2).",
                            "type": "number"
                        },
                        "base": {
                            "description": "Base (optional, lower left corner, coordinate axis 3).",
                            "type": [
                                "number",
                                "null"
                            ],
                            "default": null
                        },
                        "height": {
                            "description": "Height (optional, upper right corner, coordinate axis 3).",
                            "type": [
                                "number",
                                "null"
                            ],
                            "default": null
                        },
                        "crs": {
                            "description": "Coordinate reference system of the extent, specified as as [EPSG code](http://www.epsg-registry.org/) or [WKT2 CRS string](http://docs.opengeospatial.org/is/18-010r7/18-010r7.html). Defaults to `4326` (EPSG code 4326) unless the client explicitly requests a different coordinate reference system.",
                            "anyOf": [
                                {
                                    "title": "EPSG Code",
                                    "type": "integer",
                                    "subtype": "epsg-code",
                                    "minimum": 1000,
                                    "examples": [
                                        3857
                                    ]
                                },
                                {
                                    "title": "WKT2",
                                    "type": "string",
                                    "subtype": "wkt2-definition"
                                }
                            ],
                            "default": 4326
                        }
                    }
                },
                {
                    "title": "Vector data cube",
                    "description": "Limits the data cube to the bounding box of the given geometries in the vector data cube. For raster data, all pixels inside the bounding box that do not intersect with any of the polygons will be set to no data (`null`). Empty geometries are ignored.",
                    "type": "object",
                    "subtype": "datacube",
                    "dimensions": [
                        {
                            "type": "geometry"
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "title": "No filter",
                    "description": "Don't filter spatially. All data is included in the data cube.",
                    "type": "null"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "name": "temporal_extent",
            "description": "Temporal extent specified as two-element array with start and end date/date-time.",
            "schema": {
                "type": "array",
                "subtype": "temporal-interval",
                "uniqueItems": true,
                "minItems": 2,
                "maxItems": 2,
                "items": {
                    "anyOf": [
                        {
                            "type": "string",
                            "subtype": "date-time",
                            "format": "date-time"
                        },
                        {
                            "type": "string",
                            "subtype": "date",
                            "format": "date"
                        },
                        {
                            "type": "null"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            }
        }
    ]
